WEBVTT

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.080
The world is awash in pain.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.040
Now, wars are fought between spies
over information -

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.750
in shadow wars.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.500
<i>We've got this.</i>

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.710
<i>The target's eyes haven't adjusted
to the darkness yet!</i>

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.540
<i>Today is the day, Teach!</i>

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.330
<i>We're finally going to make you admit defeat!</i>

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.540
<b>SPY CLASSROOM</b>

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.040
<b>MISSION: Flower Garden II</b>

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.710
It all started five days ago...

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.630
Defeat me.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.500
Make me say, "I surrender."

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.080
You can use whatever methods you like.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.080
Come up with plans as a group,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.380
and take me down by the end of the month.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.130
That concludes the lesson.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.080
So, what was that about?

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.290
Ah, I see.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.250
It will be a simulation of actual combat conditions.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:12.880
We could dig up dirt.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.130
Physically restrain him.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.500
Take his friends or loved ones hostage.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:21.920
In the world of espionage, spies are often asked
to manipulate and cajole their targets.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.540
I suspect that's what this training is about.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:27.420
He said we could use whatever
methods we liked, right?

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.580
That's what I heard too, yo!

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.960
That's all well and good, but...

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.670
It was Klaus, right?

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.420
Feels like that guy...

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.040
...thinks we're a fuckin' joke!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.960
Like he can walk all over us,
just 'cuz we're washouts!

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.330
Come on, everyone.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.580
I'm sure that's not what he-

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.580
Well, I say we teach him a lesson
and show him just how strong we are.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.960
Yeah!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.670
Seven against one will hardly make for decent training.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.210
We can just win by sheer numbers!

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.000
Let's all go attack him together!

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.540
Are there any more complaints about my lesson plan?

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.830
No, sir.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.040
Good.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.130
Next time, make sure to actually use your heads.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:19.170
That marked the start of our radical new
Defeat Teach curriculum, but...

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.250
For the next five days,
all we did was rack up one loss after another.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.880
<i>We've got this.</i>

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.170
<i>The target's eyes haven't adjusted
to the darkness yet!</i>

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.960
<i>Today is the day, Teach!</i>

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.750
<i>We're finally going to make you admit defeat!</i>

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.420
Hope you're-

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:11.960
Hope you're read-

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.710
Damn it, Lily!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.290
Hey! Keep your hands to yourself!

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.880
I ain't touchin' shit!

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:21.170
It's not my fault your tits are so damn big.
S-settle down. The target has no clothes, let alone a weapon.<b></b>

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:25.880
Magnificent.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.920
By my count, that makes thirteen attempts.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.170
I applaud your tenacity.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.250
That said, your plans still need work.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:40.290
When you attack someone, you need to be
as sharp as a wind racing through a valley.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.960
At least put on a towel!

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.170
There's no need.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:47.130
A first-rate spy thinks nothing of
being seen in the nude.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.670
I'm heading out.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.000
I'll return tonight.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.380
When I do, I expect you to launch another attack.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.540
It was right there in front of my face!

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.460
He's toying with us.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.080
Shit, and with that smug-ass look on his face, too.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.080
At this rate, the month's gonna end before we know it.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.210
And when it does, we're gonna go
on that Impossible Mission...

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.630
...and get slaughtered.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.210
Each and every one of us.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.420
Monika...

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.380
At the same time,
it's too late to go back to our academies.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.040
We're boxed in.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.460
That Klaus punk...

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.330
With skills like his, I bet he's never even
been in a bind like ours.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.540
I agree.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.710
He probably can't empathize with
the worries of washouts like us at all.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:32.960
That's not true.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.880
Not at all.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.000
He might not show it, but I think Teach has
burdens of his own he's carrying.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:44.630
Lily?

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.710
We'll resume our lesson when he gets back.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.580
Before that, though,
I have a suggestion to make as your leader.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.750
Leader, huh?

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.500
For the record, I don't remember
ever signing off on that.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.880
C'mon, don't be like that!

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.960
Here, have a financier with your tea.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.000
What is that supposed to be, a bribe?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.670
I'll have one, Leader.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.210
Yeah, Leader, me too.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.500
Sellouts, the lot of you.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.290
Would you like some more tea, Monika?

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:23.040
There's new information regarding
your Impossible Mission.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.290
Understood.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:30.960
How are the girls holding up?

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.540
I understand you've been having
a hard time teaching them.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.040
Nothing gets past you, does it, C?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:40.790
I guess you're not in charge of the Cabinet Office's
Foreign Intelligence Office for nothing.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:44.080
You're a good spy, Klaus,

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.920
but your stubbornness causes headaches
for the people around you.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:50.790
You need to make sure you're doing
everything you can to assuage the girls' fears.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.170
I don't need you to tell me that-

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.790
Oh, I think I do.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:58.790
I used to be able to count on your team
to get through to you, but they're gone now.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.290
How about this, Idiot Pupil?

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:12.960
If you make it back alive, I've got a new title for you:

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.920
The Greatest Spy in the World.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.960
I'd say you will have earned it.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.040
It's got a nice ring to it, don't you think?

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.330
Magnificent.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.960
You don't want to flee?

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.290
Not in the slightest.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:34.250
You took me in when I was an orphan
and raised me to be a spy,

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.170
and I can never thank the boss enough for hiring me.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.420
It would be no exaggeration for me to say
that I love each and every person on this team.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:48.500
I'm no expert on families,
but that's what I think of you all as.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:53.130
And nothing brings me more satisfaction than
risking my life on behalf of my family.

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.960
When the hell'd you get so eloquent, Bonfire?

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:10.710
I'm back.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.630
Everyone's here, I see.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.210
Perfect.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:21.830
There's something I want to talk to you all
about regarding the mission.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:25.670
First of all, Lamplight isn't the first team
to attempt this Impossible Mission.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.710
There was another one that went before us.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.670
That team was called Inferno.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.710
I know that name.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:37.670
They're the best spy team in the Din Republic, right?

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:41.580
They're what every team in the nation aspires to be.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.000
I heard that during the Great War,
they stole intel on the Imperial army

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.960
and saved the lives of hundreds
of thousands of civilians.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.960
Wanting to join Inferno was the
reason I became a spy!

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.830
Unfortunately, Inferno is gone.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.290
It no longer exists.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:58.250
How do you know that?

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:01.080
Because only one person on the team survived.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.420
And he's standing in front of you.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:11.460
One year ago, I, code name Bonfire,

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:16.130
split off from the group and went on a solo op
per my mentor Guido's orders.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:21.080
While I was gone, the rest of Inferno's members
took on an Impossible Mission.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.750
None of them made it back alive.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.380
Inferno was like family to me.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:34.290
I wanted us to change this world,
awash in pain, together.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.630
But now, that can never happen.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:39.670
You can't be serious.
They all got wiped out?

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:42.540
You're saying they were
the best spy team in the nation...

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.880
...and they died on the very same mission
we'll be attempting in a month?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.500
I apologize for frightening you.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:53.130
As your instructor,
I make no excuses for my ineptitude.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:58.420
That said, I had a very good reason
for choosing the seven of you.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.210
I want you to come.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.420
However, I'm not going to force you.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.880
It's up to each of you to decide

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.500
if you're coming on the Impossible Mission or not.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.170
Teach...

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.330
If you wish to flee, that right is yours.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:14.750
For me, this mission is one of personal revenge.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:18.380
It's an important mission,
and the fate of our nation hangs in the balance,

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.790
but that isn't reason enough for the
seven of you to risk your lives.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.580
I'm in.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.420
You all...

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:32.500
Still, to think that you were
actually a member of Inferno.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:38.130
We had our suspicions,
but it hits different actually hearing you say it.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.330
You did?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.540
Yeah.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.330
Y'see, Lily had this idea, so we spent the afternoon...

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:48.920
...investigating Heat Haze Palace's old residents.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:56.080
We found traces from a couple people
of all sorts of ages and genders.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.540
Then, after subtly asking around
at Garmouth Seminary,

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:03.750
we obtained some testimonies that
supported our hypothesis.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:11.330
We figured that the people who lived here
must have been really important to you.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.960
You probably hit rock bottom
when you lost the people you cared about.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.210
Well, we were at rock bottom too.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.710
We're not about to abandon a fellow bottom-dweller!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.580
We're in the same hole here.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.040
Let's climb out of it together!

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:31.630
But...

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:32.830
If I may, sir!

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.290
We all feel the same way!

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:38.710
You're gonna train us up real good before the mission.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.170
Right, Bro?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.710
Naturally.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.420
Then let's do this!

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.420
We're all in?

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.540
I mean, hey, if the team leader says so.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.830
Ooh! You finally signed off on it!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.040
She was being sarcastic.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.380
Wait, that's so mean, though!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.460
It's okay, Leader, settle down.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.790
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:05.580
A good leader can't let an eensy bit
of sarcasm get to her.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:13.460
I can see I made the right choice picking you
as Lamplight's leader, Flower Garden Lily.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.330
Well, yeah, obviously!

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:16.790
In twenty days,

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:20.170
we'll be heading to the Galgad Empire
to begin the Impossible Mission.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:24.210
Until then, I'll continue forging
you all into proper spies.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:29.170
We're going to complete this mission,
and we're all going to make it back alive.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:31.420
Yes, sir!

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:42.710
When the time came,

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:46.880
Teach and the rest of us headed to where the
Impossible Mission was going to take place:

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.330
the Galgad Empire.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:04.380
<b>MISSION: Flower Garden II</b>

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:08.130
It's go time.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:12.920
We're going to split up and infiltrate Galgad
as two separate groups.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.580
You're coming all the way to the Empire
to watch some plays?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.500
Sounds like someone's living high on the hog.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.920
Who, little old me?

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.460
The others are in the dining car right now, but-

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:22.670
Pardon me...

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.460
Ah, they're back.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:30.290
As team leader, Lily, you're going to be
spearheading one of the groups,

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.210
while I lead up the other one.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.040
So, you're a wood engraver?

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.250
Indeed, I am.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:37.920
Wow, that's impressive.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.790
My apprentices do me proud.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.790
From here on out, we'll be operating separately.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.460
Any last things you want to say to me?

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:06.130
I'll save them for the next time we see each other.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.750
Until we're done here,

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.790
I'm going to avoid making contact with
anyone besides the Intel squad.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.750
We should head out, too.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.540
Our job is to steal a sample from a lab
on the Imperial capital's outskirts.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.460
Yup, that's an Impossible Mission.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.000
The Endy Laboratory, huh?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.330
Officially, the lab belongs to a
pharmaceutical company,

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.580
but in truth...

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:51.830
...the Imperial army secretly uses it to conduct
cutting-edge weapons research.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:52.830
Indeed.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.880
Naturally, security there is tight.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:59.040
Everything is going to hinge on how much
intel we can gather ahead of time.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:08.080
The two of us on the Intel squad will start
by gathering information.

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.130
And over on the Specialist squad,

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.710
we'll use our special talents
to support the other squads, yo!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.250
I'm counting on you, Mr. Bernard.

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:40.420
It says the Intel squad's used their
data to identify a key player,

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:43.330
and they want the Operations squad,
which is to say "us," to make contact.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.040
Cool, then I'm gonna go do my own thing solo.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.040
Wh-

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.630
It'll be more efficient.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.960
This way, I'll be able to help the entire team out.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:59.040
I swear, she thinks she's better than us
just 'cuz she's better than us.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.250
What about Klaus?
Can we get him to help us out?

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:04.670
"I'm devoting all my efforts
to providing backup," he said.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.130
He also said...

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:12.880
As far as specifics go, Intel should make
like a rose proudly blooming.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.830
Operations should zoop-zoop-zoop around,

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:18.290
and the Specialist squad should watch over you
as they would a baby bird.

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.330
I want everyone giving it their all.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.000
Yeesh, this is like some sorta sick joke.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.380
Don't worry!

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:28.790
We trained our butts off for this, remember?

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:30.290
We've got this!

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.670
We won't let anyone call us washouts again!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.630
Heh, easy peasy.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.210
Wait, what's that?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.710
A dummy.
This one here's the real one.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.920
Klaus pulled the same trick on me once.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.670
Looks like our training is paying off.

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:53.420
That guy was a drug dealer.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:57.040
We should find some of the lab's staff
on the client list in here.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.250
Hold it there, you two.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.290
You're tourists, I take it?

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:06.750
Sorry, but this is a prime area for pickpockets.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.750
I'm going to have to check your bags, just in case.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.290
But we, uh...

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.290
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.210
<i>I could put them to sleep and we could escape,</i>

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.960
<i>but then the cops would start looking for us...</i>

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:25.170
She's clean.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:26.960
Same here.

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.330
Thank you so much for cooperating.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:30.790
I hope you two enjoy your trip.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.080
Sybilla, where'd you hide the-

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:36.290
I didn't.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:38.630
Someone stole my stolen wallet.

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:41.750
There's only one dude I know who
could pull off a stunt like that.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.830
What a stand-up guy.
A magnificent one, even.

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:54.040
Yeah.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.420
Still, I was scared stiff back there.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:00.250
Sooner or later, our luck's gonna run out.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:07.000
As things stand, I worry that some of us
won't last until the main operation...

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:25.670
Is that from Klaus?

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:27.920
No, it's from Lily.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.460
I have the wine you ordered, sir.

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:39.920
Come in.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.170
That is an excellent disguise,

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.500
but I don't see why you felt the need
to remove your mask.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.040
I don't like to cross-dress around you, Boss.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.080
Well, suit yourself.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:00.460
What is all that?!

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:03.130
High-level Imperial classified information.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.460
You collected that all on your own?

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:12.420
I'm impressed at how much intel
you girls have collected, too.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.710
And in such a short time, no less.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:18.540
I see we have confirmation that the sample
hasn't been moved from the Endy Laboratory.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.750
I have another piece of news for you as well, Boss.

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:27.630
Our leader, Lily, was asking about us possibly holding
a party the night before the operation...

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.330
Boss?

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.000
My ears must be failing me.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.920
Did you say "a party"?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.080
According to her message, she wants us all
to gather and share a meal together.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:39.710
Has she forgotten that we're spies in hostile territory?

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:43.500
That girl's shamelessness knows no bounds.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:47.040
I believe she's worried about the team's fatigue levels.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.960
And I share her concerns.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:51.580
Ah, I see.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:55.580
For the rest of you, this is your first real mission.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.460
The exhaustion is starting to get to you all.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.710
I'll make a reservation at a
trustworthy restaurant, then.

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:02.210
Go ahead and have your party.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:03.920
Just make sure you don't get tailed.

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:04.920
If I may!

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:07.670
If it's only us, then there's a faint possibility
that something could go wrong.

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:08.880
Then call off the party.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:12.210
But if you joined us, that problem would be resolved.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.460
We wouldn't be in any danger.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.750
Cheers!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:20.540
Thanks for convincing him, Grete!

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:24.080
Sup!

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:25.830
Hey, you made it!

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.000
What are you three doing,
getting started all on your own?

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.500
Don't worry about it.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.500
Klaus'll be here soon.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:44.330
<i>I did some recon on the restaurant.</i>

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.670
<i>If I keep watch from up here, everything will be fine.</i>

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:52.630
<i>Still, I'm not nearly as invincible as they think I am.</i>

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:54.380
<i>After all,</i>

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.750
<i>against him, I've never once...</i>

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:08.580
What the...

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:16.290
Do you not understand the situation we're in?

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:18.420
How are you not more stressed?

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:19.670
Stressed?

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.290
We're stressed as hell.

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.500
But...

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:25.920
I mean, of course we are.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:28.330
How could we not be scared?

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:33.880
We've been shakin' in our boots
since the minute we left Din.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:35.830
Then, how?

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:40.330
Cuz you said you'd come today, that's how.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.330
You're late, FYI.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.170
That's why we figured we'd be fine.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:48.540
Your strength is the one thing...

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.170
we believe in.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:55.330
At least pretend to be on guard.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:58.210
This is important, Klaus.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:01.710
When someone lets you watch them sleep,

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:03.540
it's a sign of how much they trust you.

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:07.630
So, if anyone lets you see them like that,

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:09.750
make sure you do whatever it takes to protect them.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:14.330
<i>Why is it that looking at them</i>

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.630
<i>reminds me so much of Inferno?</i>

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.830
<i>Whatever the reason, though,</i>

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.630
<i>I feel like my resolve is firmer now.</i>

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.210
Wait, when did he bail on us?!

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:27.540
And what's that?

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:31.670
It's from Teach.

00:21:31.670 --> 00:21:33.330
"Change of plans."

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.000
"We talked about you going in from the east

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.210
and me from the west, but we're reversing that."

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:43.080
"Furthermore, I know it couldn't have been easy

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:45.750
having with a boss who couldn't teach or explain things."

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:46.960
"You have my thanks."

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.000
For real?

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:51.460
We never managed to make him say "I surrender"...

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.420
...but at least we got him to say "thank you".

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:56.250
That airhead actually thanked us.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.710
He could have easily been doing it on a whim.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:03.170
Oh, probably.

00:22:07.210 --> 00:22:10.250
<i>Thinking back now, though,</i>

00:22:10.920 --> 00:22:15.790
<i>that might have been the moment that us
Lamplight girls and Teach truly became a team.</i>

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:20.710
There it is, the Endy Laboratory.

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:26.040
That's where they're hiding the sample that
we need to steal back for our mission.

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:33.170
As you're aware, Klaus,

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.250
there is a postwar international treaty
banning the use of biological weapons.

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:42.790
However, it doesn't ban their development.

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:49.380
Or at least, that's how the imbeciles
in our army chose to interpret it.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:53.460
After they went ahead and continued their research,
a Galgad spy stole one of their samples.

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:57.790
According to our lab boys, it should take Galgad
a year to analyze the compound.

00:22:57.790 --> 00:23:02.710
However, we've received word from one of our
collaborators in their capital, Darton,

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:05.540
that the Imperial research efforts are
proceeding faster than anticipated.

00:23:05.540 --> 00:23:06.540
At this rate...

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:09.330
...the casualty count could well reach into the millions.

00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:15.580
The Empire has no qualms about getting
innocent civilians caught up in their assassinations.

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:19.880
I need you and the girls to retrieve that bioweapon.

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:22.330
It's a killer virus, and its name...

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:28.630
...is Abyss Doll.
